{{Quote|My bedtime stories were tales of bloody pirate raids. My friends were grizzled murderers who taught me how to punch. My jump rope was a garrote. But it was better than the orphanage.|Bazine Netal|<ref name="PerfectWeapon" />}}
'''Bazine Netal''' was an alias used by a [[human]] [[Gender|female]] [[mercenary]]. Born on the [[Inner Rim Territories|Inner Rim]] [[Planet|world]] [[Chaaktil]], she was raised in an orphanage and began training under the former [[Kanjiklub]] [[pirate]] [[Delphi Kloda]] at his [[Delphi Kloda's combat school|combat school]]. Eventually, she became a [[bounty hunter]] and eventually [[Death|killed]] her former mentor Kloda during a [[Mission to Vashka|mission]]. She was present in [[Takodana Castle]] approximately thirty [[Standard year|years]] after the [[Battle of Endor]]. Netal informed the [[First Order]] of the presence of [[BB-8]] in [[Maz Kanata|Kanata's]] castle.

==Biography==
===Early life===
The [[human]] who later adopted the alias Bazine Netal was [[Reproduction|born]] on the<ref name="PerfectWeapon" /> [[Inner Rim Territories|Inner Rim]]<ref name="Traveler's Guide">''[[Star Wars: Galaxy's Edge: Traveler's Guide to Batuu]]''</ref> [[planet]] [[Chaaktil]]<ref name="PerfectWeapon" /> in [[2 BBY]]<ref name="Timelines" /> with a name that she later kept secret. As a [[Youngling|child]], she was taken from an [[Chaako City orphanage|orphanage]] in [[Chaako City]] by [[Delphi Kloda]] and raised in Kloda's [[Delphi Kloda's combat school|combat school]], where she learned a range of deadly [[Unarmed combat|martial arts]]. There, Kloda nicknamed her "[[Chaakrabbit]]."<ref name="PerfectWeapon" />

===First assignment===
Reaching fourteen [[Standard year|years]] of age, Kloda sent her to steal an item from [[Delphi Kloda's competitor|one of his competitors]]. This was quickly discovered by her mark, who singed the inexperienced learner with a [[flamethrower]]. Despite this, she was able to [[Death|kill]] her attacker and complete her goal, though she was left with burn scars on the left side of her scalp.<ref name="PerfectWeapon" />

Thereafter, "Chaakrabbit" became a feared [[bounty hunter]] and master of disguise, learning from [[teacher]]s other than Kloda as well. At some point, she adopted the pseudonym "Bazine Netal." She based her operations on Chaaktil around [[Suli's cantina]].<ref name="PerfectWeapon" />

===Mission to Vashka===
[[File:Bazine_Netal_EaW.png|thumb|left|220px|Netal during a mission.]]
Six years after leaving Chaako [[City]], Netal received an assignment from an anonymous client. Her assignment was to retrieve a [[steel]] case which was in the possession of former [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[stormtrooper]] [[Jor Tribulus]]. Netal's client warned her that a competitor known as "[[Narglatch]]" would also be hunting for the case.<ref name="PerfectWeapon" />

Netal visited Kloda in order to borrow his [[Starship|ship]], the ''[[Sparrowhawk]]''. Kloda leant her the vessel on the condition that she take Kloda's student, the skilled [[Pantoran]] [[slicer]] [[Orri Tenro]], along on her mission as a part of his training. Reluctantly, Netal agreed, hoping that Tenro's slicing ability would outweigh the risk he posed to her [[Mission to Vashka|mission]]. As they left for the planet [[Vashka]], Tenro proved to be incompetent with anything aside from [[computer]]s.<ref name="PerfectWeapon" />

On Vashka, Netal and Tenro infiltrated the [[Vashka City Medcenter One|medcenter]] where Tribulus was most recently recorded as a patient. There they were able to learn the location of Tribulus's [[Vashka Valley Retirement Facility 48|retirement facility]]. Before disembarking for that site, Netal injected Tenro with a [[poison]] which rendered him unconscious.<ref name="PerfectWeapon" />

Netal discovered that the retirement home had been overtaken by [[Vashkan apidactyl|apidactyls]]. She made her way inside the building by distracting the apidactyls with a [[thermal detonator]]. There she met [[Aric Nightdrifter]], a retired stormtrooper who had been living in the building, and he led her to Tribulus's remains.<ref name="PerfectWeapon" />

Netal was taken by surprise when Kloda appeared and revealed that he was Narglatch, and he had raised Netal for the sole purpose of sending her after the case in order to steal it himself. After taking the case from Tribulus's corpse and disarming Netal, Kloda trapped Netal in the grave of apidactyl [[wax]] and escaped.<ref name="PerfectWeapon" />

Using the materials Nightdrifter had buried with Tribulus, Netal was able to escape the building. She threw a [[detonator]] ahead of Kloda's narglatch, creating a hole in the ground and trapping Kloda. After a brief struggle, Netal killed Kloda and returned to the ''Sparrowhawk'' with the case.<ref name="PerfectWeapon" />

===Time on Takodana===
{{Quote|Inform the First Order&hellip; I've found the droid.|translated=1|Bazine Netal, to the First Order|<ref name="TFA" />}}
[[File:Bazine_reporting.png|thumb|right|250px|Netal reported a sighting of BB-8 to the First Order.]]
During the [[First Order]]'s [[Cold War|conflict]] with the [[Resistance]],<ref name="TFA" /> Netal served as a [[spy]] with a direct line to the First Order. Located at [[Maz Kanata]]'s [[Takodana Castle|castle]] on [[Takodana]],<ref name="TFAVD">''[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> Netal posed as [[Grummgar]]'s girlfriend.<ref name="Geektionary">''[[Star Wars: Geektionary: The Galaxy from A - Z]]''</ref>

As the ''[[Millennium Falcon]]''{{'s}} [[captain]] [[Han Solo]] arrived there with the fugitives [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]], [[Finn]], and [[BB-8]] in [[34 ABY]], she informed the Order of the wanted [[droid]]'s sighting, just as a Resistance-sympathetic spy informed its organization likewise. Soon, the [[First Order military]] [[Battle of Takodana|assaulted]] the site, ultimately sparking the first battle of the [[First Order-Resistance War]].<ref name="TFA" />

===Searching for the ''Millennium Falcon''===
{{Quote|Because you have something I need&mdash;information. I'm looking for the ''Millennium Falcon'', and rumor is that you nearly caught it.|Bazine Netal, to IG-88|<ref name="Flight of the Falcon 1">{{IDWAdventuresCite-2017|issue=14|story=Flight of the Falcon, Part 1: Spy Games}}</ref>}}
[[File:BazineNetalandIG-88.jpg|thumb|left|249x249px|Netal and IG-88 discussing the ''Millennium Falcon''.]]
Later, Netal was hired by a employer to search for the ''Millennium Falcon''. She heard a rumor that [[IG-88B|IG-88]] nearly caught it, so she met with IG-88 to discuss about the ''Millennium Falcon''. During their discussion, IG-88 told Netal the story of when he almost caught the ''Falcon'' with [[Agent]] [[Alexsandr Kallus|Kallus]]. IG-88 also told Netal that he almost had the ''Millennium Falcon'' again, but the bounty hunter [[Boba Fett]] got to Solo and the ''Falcon'' first. Netal responded that IG-88 had a lot of excuses and that her employer only paid for results. Before she left to continue her search, Netal informed IG-88 that someone knew where the ''Falcon'' was and that they would tell her where it was.<ref name="Flight of the Falcon 1" />

Netal later met with two droids, [[Doc]] and [[Teetee]]. They told Netal a story of when they encountered the ''Millennium Falcon'' on [[Lotho Minor]]. After the story, Netal told them that it wasn't even close to what she wanted. When she asked where she could find the ''Falcon'', the pair didn't know as they hadn't seen it since Lotho Minor. Netal became angry but Teetee said that he knew the bounty hunter [[Embo]] had come into contact with her quarry. Netal left the droids and went to find Embo.<ref name="Flight of the Falcon 2">{{IDWAdventuresCite-2017|issue=15|story=Flight of the Falcon, Part 2: The Planet of Misfit Droids}}</ref>

Netal made her way to [[Felucia]] where she found Embo. Knowing that Embo's funding from the [[New Republic]] had stopped, she made a deal with the [[Kyuzo]] where in exchange for [[Galactic Credit Standard|credits]], he would give her information she needed, about his encounter with the ''Millennium Falcon''. After Embo told Netal a story of when he failed to capture the ''Falcon'' on a [[Unidentified space station (Lando Calrissian)|space station]] not long after the [[Battle of Endor]], Netal questioned why it had been so hard to capture one ship. Following Embo's response, Netal replied that she would do more than try and capture it, she would succeed. After paying Embo the credits they agreed upon, he told her that he had heard the ship had surfaced somewhere. Finding the information from Embo interesting, Netal added that if there was anyone that wanted to capture the ''Falcon'' as much as her employer, it would be "her". Netal then set off for her next destination.<ref name="Home Again">{{IDWAdventuresCite-2017|issue=16|story=Flight of the Falcon, Part 3: Home Again}}</ref>

[[File:BazineandProxima.jpg|thumb|235x235px|Netal and Proxima discussing about the ''Millennium Falcon''.]]
After arriving on [[Corellia]], Netal captured one of the most skilled [[White Worms]] children so she could talk to [[Lady]] [[Proxima]] about the ''Millennium Falcon''. She threatened to kill Proxima and the skilled child if she didn't tell her about the ''Millennium Falcon''. Proxima told Netal a story of when Han returned to Corellia for parts for the ''Millennium Falcon''. During this, [[Moloch]], who served the White Worms, captured Han and [[Chewbacca]] and brought them to Proxima. Proxima told Han he would be punished because he owed her [[coaxium]] and had given her face scars from the sunlight. Chewbacca gave Han a thermal detonator which he used to explode the window which brought in sunlight. The sunlight damaged Proxima's face again and blinded her right [[eye]] as Han and Chewbacca made their escape. After the story, Netal became frustrated about that they did not capture the ''Millennium Falcon''. Proxima suggested that Netal visit [[Gannis Ducain]] on [[Jakku]], as she understood he had gotten his hands on the ''Falcon'' at one point.<ref name="Lady and the Tramp">{{IDWAdventuresCite-2017|issue=17|story=Flight of the Falcon, Part 4: Lady and the Tramp}}</ref>

Netal found Ducain and was told his story of how he stole the ''Falcon'' from Solo and its [[time]] with him, ultimately learning that Ducain was trying to return it to Solo, before the Irving Boys stole it from him. After the story, Ducain left to join the Resistance and Netal became mad. As she left, Proxima contacted Netal saying that she had found the ''Falcon'' and that Netal should find [[Hondo Ohnaka]] on [[Batuu]] with it.<ref name="Grand Theft Falcon">{{IDWAdventuresCite-2017|issue=18|story=Flight of the Falcon, Part 5: Grand Theft Falcon}}</ref>

==Personality and traits==
[[File:PreemptiveStrike-Leg.png|thumb|left|220px|Bazine Netal was elusive and calculating.]]
Bazine Netal was intelligent and calculating, traits that served her well in her job. She was also elusive, as she was skilled at playing lowly [[alien]]s and would not reveal her past to anyone.<ref name="PerfectWeapon" />

Bazine Netal was a [[human]] female<ref name="PerfectWeapon" /> who stood at 1.7 [[meter]]s.<ref name="ECUC" /> She had [[Color|black]] [[hair]], dark [[eye]]s,<ref name="PerfectWeapon" /> and light skin.<ref name="TFA" />

==Equipment==
Netal used [[Rishi eel ink]] to conceal her fingerprints. She also kept several small thermal detonators inside the hollow wedges of her [[boot]]s.<ref name="PerfectWeapon" />

==Behind the scenes==
Bazine Netal first appeared in the short story "[[The Perfect Weapon]]," written by [[Delilah S. Dawson]].<ref name="PerfectWeapon" /> She was portrayed by [[Anna Brewster]] in [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']].<ref name="TFA" />

